## Bug Description

In `numpy/_core/src/multiarray/methods.c`, after `Py_INCREF(typecode)` at line 2100, four early `return NULL` paths skip the matching `Py_DECREF(typecode)`, leaking the reference.

## Location

`numpy/_core/src/multiarray/methods.c:2100-2131`

## Code

```c
Py_INCREF(typecode);        // line 2100: refcount incremented

if (nd < 0) {
    return NULL;            // line 2103: typecode LEAKED
}
// ...
if (dimensions[i] < 0) {
    return NULL;            // line 2118: typecode LEAKED
}
// ...
if (overflow) {
    PyErr_NoMemory();
    return NULL;            // line 2123: typecode LEAKED
}
// ...
if (!PyList_Check(rawdata)) {
    return NULL;            // line 2131: typecode LEAKED
}
```

## Impact

Every failed ndarray unpickling operation leaks the `typecode` reference. This affects `pickle.loads()` / `numpy.loads()` on corrupted or malformed ndarray pickle data.

## Suggested Fix

Replace all early `return NULL` with `goto fail` where `fail` does `Py_DECREF(typecode)`:

```c
fail:
    Py_DECREF(typecode);
    return NULL;
```

## Environment

- NumPy version: current main
- Affected: `ndarray.__setstate__()` (unpickling)

## Bug Description

In `numpy/_core/src/multiarray/descriptor.c`, `PyArray_DiscoverDTypeFromScalarType` returns a new reference, but `PyArray_GetDefaultDescr` does NOT steal it. The `DType` reference is leaked unconditionally.

## Location

`numpy/_core/src/multiarray/descriptor.c:1599-1601`

## Code

```c
PyObject *DType = PyArray_DiscoverDTypeFromScalarType(typ);  // NEW REF
if (DType != NULL) {
    return PyArray_GetDefaultDescr((PyArray_DTypeMeta *)DType);  // DType LEAKED!
}
```

## Impact

`PyArray_GetDefaultDescr` returns a new reference (via `Py_INCREF` or `NPY_DT_CALL_default_descr`). It does NOT steal the `DType` reference. Therefore `DType` is leaked on every successful call to `_convert_from_type` with a scalar type. This triggers on every custom scalar type → dtype conversion.

## Suggested Fix

```c
PyObject *DType = PyArray_DiscoverDTypeFromScalarType(typ);
if (DType != NULL) {
    PyArray_Descr *ret = PyArray_GetDefaultDescr((PyArray_DTypeMeta *)DType);
    Py_DECREF(DType);
    return ret;
}
```

## Environment

- NumPy version: current main
- Affected: `numpy.dtype()` conversions from custom scalar types
